import{_t as e,at as t,et as n,it as r,n as i,ot as a,rt as o,xt as s}from"./chunks/framework.C1oW5ckO.js";var c=JSON.parse(`{"title":"TabDisplay","description":"","frontmatter":{"navigation":{"category":"Gameplay"},"editLink":"https://github.com/filiphsps/pumpkin-plugins/edit/master/packages/tab-display/docs/index.md"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"packages/tab-display/docs/index.md","filePath":"packages/tab-display/docs/index.md","lastUpdated":1791738437000}`),l={name:`packages/tab-display/docs/index.md`},u={id:`tabdisplay`,tabindex:`-1`,class:`component-page-title`},d={class:`component-page-title__version`};function f(i,c,l,f,p,m){let h=s(`Badge`);return e(),o(`div`,null,[n(`h1`,u,[c[0]||=n(`img`,{class:`component-page-title__icon`,src:`/pumpkin-plugins/packages/tab-display/icon.svg`,alt:``,"aria-hidden":`true`,width:`48`,height:`48`},null,-1),c[1]||=n(`span`,{class:`component-page-title__text`},[t(`TabDisplay `),n(`a`,{class:`header-anchor`,href:`#tabdisplay`,"aria-label":`Permalink to “TabDisplay”`},`​`)],-1),n(`span`,d,[a(h,{type:`info`,text:`v0.0.0`})])]),c[2]||=r(`<p>TabDisplay customizes Pumpkin&#39;s native Java player list with formatted real-player names and per-viewer headers and footers. It keeps the native roster and latency behavior. Bedrock players continue to see Pumpkin&#39;s unchanged player list.</p><p>Install <code>tab-display.wasm</code> in the server&#39;s <code>plugins/</code> directory and restart. TabDisplay creates <code>plugins/data/TabDisplay/config.toml</code>. It requests <code>fs.read.data</code> and <code>fs.write.data</code> for that file; the normal Pumpkin Market update check also requests <code>http.outbound</code>.</p><h2 id="current-capability-boundary" tabindex="-1">Current capability boundary <a class="header-anchor" href="#current-capability-boundary" aria-label="Permalink to “Current capability boundary”">​</a></h2><p>The Java adapter currently makes tab-name and header/footer calls only for Java protocol <code>v-26-3</code>. It leaves other Java versions unchanged and reports them as unsupported in <code>/tabdisplay status</code>. These adapter calls have not been verified with a live Java client in this environment. Status and documentation do not claim that a live client displayed the result.</p><p>Native sorting is disabled. Non-empty <code>sorting.rules</code> values fail config validation because the client&#39;s ordering direction has not been verified. Numeric objectives are also rejected until their player-list display behavior is verified. The Bedrock adapter does not send Java tab fields or modify names, scores, identities, skins or roster membership.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Current behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Java row names</td><td>Global subject formatting, gated to <code>v-26-3</code>; live client behavior unverified</td></tr><tr><td>Java header/footer</td><td>Per-viewer formatted lines, gated to <code>v-26-3</code>; live client behavior unverified</td></tr><tr><td>Java sorting</td><td>Disabled; config rejects non-empty rules</td></tr><tr><td>Java numeric objective</td><td>Disabled; config rejects <code>objective.enabled = true</code></td></tr><tr><td>Bedrock roster</td><td>Left unchanged; objective and row formatting unsupported</td></tr><tr><td>Per-viewer row names, fake rows and fixed slots</td><td>Not implemented</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="pumpkinpie-placeholders" tabindex="-1">PumpkinPIE placeholders <a class="header-anchor" href="#pumpkinpie-placeholders" aria-label="Permalink to “PumpkinPIE placeholders”">​</a></h2><p>PumpkinPIE is optional. TabDisplay talks to the configured plugin name through the shared PumpkinPIE API and does not require the provider as plugin metadata. If it is absent, the display commands still work and templates use the configured <code>placeholders.missing_provider</code> fallback (<code>literal</code> by default, or <code>empty</code>). Once the provider returns, one shared session resumes bounded placeholder work. Unknown identifiers follow <code>placeholders.unresolved</code>.</p><p>Install only a PumpkinPIE artifact compatible with the server and plugin API versions. Confirm its release provenance from the provider&#39;s official distribution before installing it; no provider source or binary is bundled here. Real-IPC integration against a provenance-verified provider artifact is still pending.</p><p>Header and footer templates use the viewer&#39;s context. A row-name template uses the listed subject&#39;s context. Placeholders receive a player&#39;s current name only at the request boundary; internal state uses UUIDs. Provider output is rendered as literal text and cannot inject formatting JSON or clickable commands.</p><h2 id="configuration-and-ownership" tabindex="-1">Configuration and ownership <a class="header-anchor" href="#configuration-and-ownership" aria-label="Permalink to “Configuration and ownership”">​</a></h2><p>Use <code>/tabdisplay reload</code> to validate and apply <code>config.toml</code>. Invalid TOML or unsupported settings leave the running config and file contents untouched. <code>/tabdisplay status</code> reports provider state, connected Java versions, unsupported capabilities and unresolved placeholder identifiers. <code>/tabdisplay inspect &lt;player&gt;</code> reports safe per-player context and placeholder IDs; it never displays resolved placeholder values.</p><p>The commands are operator-only by default. A row name is restored on disable, reload that turns row formatting off, disconnect or unload only while the current value still matches TabDisplay&#39;s last write. If another plugin changes the name, TabDisplay releases ownership and leaves that value alone. Headers and footers have no getter for original state in the pinned API; TabDisplay clears them to empty on disable or unload under exclusive ownership. Native order resets to zero if later enabled after a verified probe.</p><h2 id="work-limits-and-measurements" tabindex="-1">Work limits and measurements <a class="header-anchor" href="#work-limits-and-measurements" aria-label="Permalink to “Work limits and measurements”">​</a></h2><p>Defaults refresh templates every 20 ticks and snapshot at most 500 players; <code>general.max_players</code> is bounded at 5,000. Placeholder resolution processes at most 256 requests and 1 MiB per batch on a tick. Rendered fields are capped at 8 KiB. When the provider is unavailable, the last successful frame is retained for up to 30 seconds before configured fallback text is applied.</p><p>No server TPS or client display performance benchmark has been collected. The work limits bound individual snapshots and placeholder batches, but they are not a measured capacity claim.</p>`,16)])}var p=i(l,[[`render`,f]]);export{c as __pageData,p as default};